## Metal–Organic Frameworks
Topological rationalization is used to design a zeotype mesoporous Zr metal– organic framework. When tetrahedra (orange; see picture) with $[\mathsf{M}_{3}\mathsf{O}(\mathsf{C O O})_{6}]$ nodes and tridentate benzene-1,3,5-tricarboxylate faces are connected in an
eclipsed configuration ( $\left\langle D_{3h}\right.$ nodes; lightblue bar), an mtn network is formed. A $60^{\circ}$ rotation between tetrahedra gives a staggered configuration with $D_{3d}$ -connected nodes (dark-blue bar) and abcristobalite network.
